    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working correctly. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was caused by the main `frai` program consuming the `--ci` flag before the `gate` subcommand could receive it. When you ran `frai gate init --ci`, the parser would capture `--ci` at the main program level, and the gate subcommand's action handler would only receive `['init']` without the flag.\n\n**The fix:** Modified the gate command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to check `process.argv` directly for the `--ci` flag. If present after the 'gate' command, it gets added to the arguments passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 Direct `frai-gate init --ci` still works as before\n- \u2705 Package rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
